{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChFYkHLwKCwjSF77hnVeY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[x] `uninstall` makes no `hermes config set` call\n\n`hermes-tiiny-router uninstall` is done. All four checklist items pass and are committed. `npm test` passes: 12 Node tests plus the Python suite.\n\n**What it does:**\n- Removes `$HERMES_HOME/plugins/tiiny-router/` and exits 0, but only if the install manifest in that directory names this package. If the manifest is missing, can't be parsed, or names another package, it exits 1 and leaves the directory in place. The new `readManifest()` in `src/manifest.ts` does that check.\n- Never runs `hermes config` and leaves everything else in the Hermes home alone. Afterwards it prints the command to unselect the backend.\n\n**Tests** are in `test/uninstall.test.ts` and run the command as a subprocess. Two of them (the rest of the Hermes home is unchanged, and no `hermes config` call is made) passed as soon as I wrote them, because the code never did those things. To check they can actually fail, I broke the code on purpose for each one and saw it fail, then put the code back.\n\n**Choices the ticket didn't cover:**\n- If nothing is installed, `uninstall` exits 0 instead of failing, since the end state is already what the user wants. This has a test.\n- A manifest written by a different package is refused the same way as a missing one. This has a test.\n- The printed unselect command is `hermes config set delegation.backend default`. I guessed `default` because that's the value `test/install.test.ts` puts in its sample `config.yaml`. Nothing in the repo says what Hermes calls its default backend, so check this one.\n\nDuring a check I ran `git checkout` on a file to undo a deliberate break, and it also wiped my uncommitted `readManifest` code. I rewrote it and the full suite passed afterwards. I added a warning about this to `AGENTS.md`, along with a note on how `readManifest` should be used. Notes for this attempt are in `.redeye/notes.md`, which is not committed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":623,"cache_read_input_tokens":66012,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":623},"output_tokens":663,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"666abf6b-f56d-4e3d-8192-7c5721ebfd54","uuid":"ed9502ae-26a7-46e6-a507-d34ccf8a4a99","timestamp":"2026-11-21T05:49:04.636Z","request_id":"req_011ChFYkH9mja1ca4rCYf439"}
